🔧 Key Backend Concepts (FastAPI)
Each agent lives as a callable class/module. They each:

- Take input (startup config, task, prior agent outputs)
- Make a decision (name, tool, LLM call, judgment)
- Return structured data downstream

The /simulate route ties them all together:
@app.post("/simulate")
def simulate(request: StartupInput):
    strategy = StrategyAgent().run(request)
    stack = StackBuilderAgent().run(strategy)
    demo = DemoOutputAgent().run(stack, request.prompt)
    evals = EvalAgent().evaluate(request.prompt, demo)
    investor = InvestorAgent().decide(evals, strategy)

    return SimulationResult(
        output=demo,
        evals=evals,
        decision=investor,
        archetype=assign_archetype(evals)
    )


